From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:19:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] d3d12: tiled resources tier 2 through Metal placement
 sparse; report feature level 12_0

Reserved textures (2D, no MSAA) and buffers are Metal placement sparse
resources with 64 KB pages, the size of D3D12 tiles, and D3D12 heaps can now
back their tiles. UpdateTileMappings and CopyTileMappings run on a Metal 4
queue, fenced against the D3D12 queue with an event, so earlier work sees the
old mappings and later work the new ones. GetResourceTiling reports Metal's
tile shapes (the D3D12 standard shapes for 2D) and packed mip tail. With
placement sparse available (macOS 26.4+), the device reports tiled resources
tier 2 and feature level 12_0; otherwise nothing changes.

winemetal: placement sparse textures and buffers, tile size and mip tail
queries, a Metal 4 queue with mapping updates and copies, event wait/signal,
and the heap's max compatible placement sparse page size.
